cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CoRTeC: A Differentially Private Release for Synthetic Tabular Data, Decodable by Any Generator"
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying paper, please cite it."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.2.5"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22945315"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Calyie/cortec"
abstract: >-
  An institution that holds sensitive tabular data wants to train models, share samples and
  support research without exposing a record, under differential privacy. Today's methods spend
  the budget inside a fitted model or a training run, so what leaves cannot be reviewed as counts
  or reused. We propose CoRTeC, a differentially private release built for a downstream
  classifier: inside cohorts formed by a public rule or a charged procedure, the cohort size, the
  class balance, one histogram per attribute per outcome class and a table of outcome rates over
  disjoint cells, every count noised, the budget spent once, shipped for review. Everything after
  the release is post-processing: a maximum-entropy decoder reconstructs rows at no cost, a frozen
  generative model (five backbones) decodes the same release under exact per-bin counts without
  seeing a record, and a selection step rakes any decoder's pool to the released cells, so one
  release serves unlimited draws. At ε = 2 and n = 300 and 1,000, the auto-configured release
  decoded with no model trains models within 0.02 AUC of a real sample of its size on Adult over
  three splits; on NHANES and bank marketing the gap is larger, up to 0.07 AUC on the medical
  dataset at n = 300. It is level with or ahead of the reference AIM on utility in five of six
  dataset-size cells, ahead on single columns on Adult and bank, level on NHANES, and behind on
  pairs at n = 1,000 on Adult and at both sizes on NHANES; the fixed-rule release is ahead of AIM
  on the conditionals it names on Adult. Four controls attribute the rest: the language model adds
  plausibility from the column names, repairs the pairs it recognises, invents those it expects,
  and without the release recites the public file. No private row reaches any decoder, the
  strongest membership attack reaches a small fraction of the permitted advantage, and no
  synthetic row copies a training row. This repository holds the Apache-2.0 reference
  implementation with its tests, the research pipeline, the papers and the frozen auto-
  configurations.
authors:
